<!--Post: 3993--><!--Time: 1105505486-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3993"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Remember in BTK&#39;s 1974 letter, he signs off <BR>with the statment, &#34;The code word for me will be <BR>BTK, for bind them, torture them and kill them. <BR>They will be on the next victim.&#34;  Wasn&#39;t Kathryn <BR>his next victim?  Could the 3 stab wounds be <BR>his signature?  Especially since she was the <BR>only victim stabbed?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3993-->
<!--Post: 3995--><!--Time: 1105507436-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3995"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 9:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How do you know that Kathryn Bright had exactly 3 stab wounds? As far as I know that information has never been revealed. <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3995-->
<!--Post: 3998--><!--Time: 1105512524-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3998"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 10:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, at &#34;Crime Library&#34; the BTK story says this about KB: <BR> <BR>&#34;Kevin managed to escape and get help for his sister, but she died five hours after being taken to the hospital with three stab wounds in her abdomen.&#34; <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know if those were her only stab wounds or not.  They just may not have mentioned any lesser stab wounds that weren&#39;t fatal. <BR> <BR>Curious2, is that where you saw the reference to three stab wounds, at the Crime Library?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3998-->
<!--Post: 4012--><!--Time: 1105535195-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4012"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 5:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Jujuree, and also among some early  <BR>newspaper articles.  I just reread my above <BR>post, and realized I should have questioned, <BR>&#34;Could the 3 stab wounds be his carved <BR>initials?&#34; since he said they would be &#34;on <BR>his next victim.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4012-->
<!--Post: 4013--><!--Time: 1105535199-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4013"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 5:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Jujuree<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4013-->
<!--Post: 4043--><!--Time: 1105559846-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4043"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 11:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think he&#39;s shown considerable &#34;overkill&#34; in the past, making sure that his victims were dead. The three stab wounds seem almost like an afterthought compared to the other victims. This &#34;underkill&#34; suggests to me that he was freaked out about Kevin and just wanted to make sure Kathryn was out before he hightailed it. If he hasn&#39;t mentioned it extensively to the police, it may be--as others wrote--that he couldn&#39;t stay to take pictures, drawings, etc., so his memory may not be as clear and he doesn&#39;t want to show that ignorance to the police.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4043-->
